    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0339" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760D.6115/48: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-13T15:00:00+03:00">April 13, 1940—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 13—2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>379. The Moscow newspapers publish the text of an act signed at Petsamo on April
                    9 by representatives of the Red Army and of the Finnish Army, acting in
                    accordance with articles VI and VII of the Protocol appended to the peace treaty
                    between the Soviet Union and Finland, signed March 12, effecting the transfer to
                    Finnish authorities of Petsamo and the port of Liinahamari with all buildings
                    and equipment appertaining to municipal economy and local industry.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
